            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-32650",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Rustls is a modern TLS library written in Rust. `rustls::ConnectionCom ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Rustls is a modern TLS library written in Rust. `rustls::ConnectionCommon::complete_io` could fall into an infinite loop based on network input. When using a blocking rustls server, if a client send a `close_notify` message immediately after `client_hello`, the server's `complete_io` will get in an infinite loop. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.23.5, 0.22.4, and 0.21.11."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-32650",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-32650\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: rustls\nFixed Version: 0.23.5, 0.22.4, 0.21.11\nLink: [CVE-2024-32650](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-32650)\nRustls is a modern TLS library written in Rust. `rustls::ConnectionCommon::complete_io` could fall into an infinite loop based on network input. When using a blocking rustls server, if a client send a `close_notify` message immediately after `client_hello`, the server's `complete_io` will get in an infinite loop. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.23.5, 0.22.4, and 0.21.11.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-32650**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|rustls|0.23.5, 0.22.4, 0.21.11|[CVE-2024-32650](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-32650)|\n\nRustls is a modern TLS library written in Rust. `rustls::ConnectionCommon::complete_io` could fall into an infinite loop based on network input. When using a blocking rustls server, if a client send a `close_notify` message immediately after `client_hello`, the server's `complete_io` will get in an infinite loop. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.23.5, 0.22.4, and 0.21.11."
              },
